```js
updated(changedProperties) {
  if (changedProperties.has('error')) {
    // existing behaviour: mirror the error attribute onto each child
    this.items.forEach((el) => {
      if (this.error) el.setAttribute('error', '');
      else el.removeAttribute('error');
    });
  }
}

render() {
  const isInvalid = this.validity && this.validity !== 'valid';

  return html`
    <fieldset
      role="radiogroup"
      aria-invalid="${isInvalid ? 'true' : 'false'}"
      aria-describedby="${isInvalid ? 'group-error' : nothing}"
    >
      <legend><slot name="legend"></slot></legend>
      <slot></slot>
      ${this.error
        ? html`<p id="group-error" role="alert" aria-live="assertive">${this.error}</p>`
        : nothing}
    </fieldset>
  `;
}
```

Key change: `aria-invalid` is driven by `validity` (the authoritative field per the property comment), not just presence of `error` — so `valueMissing` (required-but-unanswered, no custom message) is announced too, not only `customError`. `aria-describedby` links the fieldset to the error message's `id` so screen readers announce the specific reason, not just "invalid."
